@numman-ali - I think we also need to expand the plugin to be more aligned with the model settings supported by codex cli since codex cli is using the backend-api rather than regular front-end OpenAI API endpoints. Rather than hard coding a bunch of settings in the plugin, the loader should be reading from the `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` and allowing per-model settings for reasoningEffort, reasoningSummary, and textVerbosity.

I also think that like opencode does for its zen providers, and because with the backend-api we use `store: false`, the plugin should include: ["reasoning.encrypted_content"]

[Here's a gist](https://gist.github.com/ben-vargas/af96bcc0a9788bb471a170e16f7a5d73) with more detail, I'm thinking of submitting a PR to provide less hard coding, more alignment with the OpenAI backend api used with ChatGPT OAuth like Codex CLI does and then users can go from there. It's possibly that opencode isn't implementing some of the options because its simply not available in the front-end APIs from OpenAI for gpt-5-codex, but if we can see the options being used by Codex CLI on the backend, I it should probably be offered in the loader.

